{
  "an7.74:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.74 ",
  "an7.74:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an7.74:0.3": "About Araka ",
  "an7.74:1.1": "“Once upon a time, mendicants, there was a teacher named Araka. He was a religious founder and was free of desire for sensual pleasures. ",
  "an7.74:1.2": "He had many hundreds of disciples, ",
  "an7.74:1.3": "and he taught them like this: ",
  "an7.74:1.4": "‘Brahmins, life as a human is short, brief, and fleeting, full of suffering and distress. Be thoughtful and wake up! Do what’s good and lead the spiritual life, for no one born can escape death. ",
  "an7.74:2.1": "It’s like a drop of dew on a grass tip. When the sun comes up it vanishes right away and doesn’t last long. ",
  "an7.74:2.2": "In the same way, life as a human is like a dewdrop. It’s brief and fleeting, full of suffering and distress. Be thoughtful and wake up! Do what’s good and lead the spiritual life, for no one born can escape death. ",
  "an7.74:3.1": "It’s like when the heavens rain heavily. The bubbles vanish right away and don’t last long. ",
  "an7.74:3.2": "In the same way, life as a human is like a bubble. … ",
  "an7.74:4.1": "It’s like a line drawn in water. It vanishes right away and doesn’t last long. ",
  "an7.74:4.2": "In the same way, life as a human is like a line drawn in water. … ",
  "an7.74:4.3": "",
  "an7.74:5.1": "It’s like a mountain river traveling far, flowing fast, carrying all before it. It doesn’t turn back—not for a moment, a second, an hour�